<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Expressions on STEP Batch 12</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/tags/expressions/</link><description>Recent content in Expressions on STEP Batch 12</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en_US</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:25:56 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://step-12.github.io/tags/expressions/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Functions as Values</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/intro_js/functions_as_values/</link><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:24:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/intro_js/functions_as_values/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="functions-are-values"&gt;Functions Are Values&lt;a class="anchor" href="#functions-are-values"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So far, we have been writing functions like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-javascript" data-lang="javascript"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;And when we want to use the function, we write:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-javascript" data-lang="javascript"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This works perfectly well.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But there is another way to write a function in JavaScript. Before we look at it, let&amp;rsquo;s revisit something we have already learned.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="expressions-produce-values"&gt;Expressions produce values&lt;a class="anchor" href="#expressions-produce-values"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We have spent quite some time working with expressions.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Consider:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-javascript" data-lang="javascript"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;JavaScript evaluates the expression &lt;code&gt;10 + 20&lt;/code&gt;. It produces the value &lt;code&gt;30&lt;/code&gt;, which is then associated with the name &lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>